WEBVTT

00:00:00.051 --> 00:00:02.194
Domino's Quick Starter.

00:00:02.254 --> 00:00:05.476
Lisa's Song by Leslie Thompson.

00:00:05.536 --> 00:00:07.688
Read by Richard Linson.

00:00:07.748 --> 00:00:09.100
Chris Mills.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.601
Penny Rawlins.

00:00:10.661 --> 00:00:12.132
Jane Whittenshaw.

00:00:12.192 --> 00:00:13.934
James Daniel Wilson.

00:00:13.994 --> 00:00:15.766
And Jennifer Woodward.

00:00:15.826 --> 00:00:21.131
Published in copyright, Oxford University Press 2012.

00:00:21.191 --> 00:00:23.334
Chapter One.

00:00:23.394 --> 00:00:25.055
Al's First Love.

00:00:35.632 --> 00:00:38.162
Our brown is 13.

00:00:38.222 --> 00:00:43.243
He lives with his parents in a little house.

00:00:43.303 --> 00:00:47.244
It's in Nottingham in England.

00:00:47.304 --> 00:00:50.444
The family are happy.

00:00:50.504 --> 00:00:54.025
But they have not got much money.

00:00:54.085 --> 00:00:56.596
So life is not easy.

00:00:58.856 --> 00:01:04.617
When our story begins, Mrs. Brown is expecting a baby.

00:01:06.685 --> 00:01:12.718
Al is waiting excitedly for his new little brother or sister.

00:01:12.778 --> 00:01:16.990
Al's first love is music.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.833
He can play the guitar very well.

00:01:22.954 --> 00:01:29.108
He is in a band, fast cars with three of his friends.

00:01:29.168 --> 00:01:33.280
They are Emma, Mick and Ben.

00:01:36.073 --> 00:01:40.607
Ben and Al play the guitars in the band.

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:45.580
Emma sings and Mick plays the drums.

00:01:49.963 --> 00:01:53.116
Al writes songs for the band.

00:01:53.176 --> 00:01:56.758
They play at Ben's house.

00:01:56.818 --> 00:02:02.062
Al's parents often come and listen to them.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:06.973
They are good friends with Ben's parents.

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:11.344
Our boy can't live without his music.

00:02:11.404 --> 00:02:14.175
Al's parents tell everyone.

00:02:14.235 --> 00:02:30.296
Chapter 2 Al's Baby Sister. 

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:46.296
One morning, Mrs. Brown does not feel well.

00:02:46.356 --> 00:02:50.769
The baby's coming, she says.

00:02:50.828 --> 00:02:54.191
What, it's six weeks early.

00:02:54.251 --> 00:02:56.742
Mr. Brown cries.

00:02:56.802 --> 00:02:59.594
Yes, I know.

00:02:59.654 --> 00:03:03.277
But please, take me to the hospital.

00:03:03.337 --> 00:03:06.519
This baby can't wait.

00:03:06.579 --> 00:03:10.152
Mrs. Brown is right.

00:03:10.212 --> 00:03:15.734
After six hours, Lisa arrives.

00:03:15.794 --> 00:03:21.395
She is beautiful, but she is very little.

00:03:21.455 --> 00:03:25.996
She must stay in hospital for two weeks.

00:03:28.776 --> 00:03:33.857
When Lisa comes home, life is not the same.

00:03:33.917 --> 00:03:40.113
The baby cries a lot, and she doesn't eat much.

00:03:40.173 --> 00:03:42.929
Is the little girl all right?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.291
Everyone is tired.

00:03:48.351 --> 00:03:58.335
When Al tries to play his guitar, his mother says, Shh, Lisa's sleeping.

00:03:58.395 --> 00:04:04.498
Mr. Brown says, You must help more in the house, Al.

00:04:04.558 --> 00:04:07.379
Your mother's very tired.

00:04:07.439 --> 00:04:10.054
Al tries to help.

00:04:10.114 --> 00:04:12.928
But he is tired too.

00:04:12.988 --> 00:04:19.510
He can't concentrate at school and he forgets to do his homework.

00:04:23.011 --> 00:04:28.683
One day Al visits his grandfather Jack Brown.

00:04:28.743 --> 00:04:32.334
The old man lives alone.

00:04:32.394 --> 00:04:38.320
Al says Mum and Dad never listen to me now.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.431
They're always with Lisa.

00:04:42.712 --> 00:04:48.516
A new baby is a lot of work. Jack says.
 
00:04:48.576 --> 00:04:52.678
You must understand that, Al.

00:04:52.738 --> 00:04:55.350
But what about you?

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:58.622
Are you writing any new songs?

00:04:58.682 --> 00:05:02.100
You're a good songwriter.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:06.259
Al says nothing to his grandfather.

00:05:06.319 --> 00:05:09.921
He has no time for the band these days.

00:05:12.683 --> 00:05:18.366
When Jack is alone, he takes out an old photograph.

00:05:18.426 --> 00:05:20.798
He looks at it.

00:05:20.858 --> 00:05:24.890
It is a picture of his sister, Alice.

00:05:27.271 --> 00:05:30.053
Life's short, Al?

00:05:30.113 --> 00:05:32.188
He says quietly.

00:05:32.248 --> 00:05:35.544
Be good to your sister.

00:05:35.604 --> 00:05:41.729
You're older, but you don't always know best.

00:05:41.788 --> 00:06:08.100
Chapter 3. Al's Angry Friends. 

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:13.818
Al's friends are waiting for him at Ben's house.

00:06:13.878 --> 00:06:17.462
Al is late again.

00:06:17.522 --> 00:06:21.836
Where is he? Emma asks.
  
00:06:21.896 --> 00:06:26.000
We can't begin playing without him.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:29.463
He's always late these days.

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:31.915
Ben says angrily.

00:06:31.975 --> 00:06:35.067
And he can't concentrate.

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:38.698
Let's look for a different guitar player.

00:06:38.758 --> 00:06:42.119
My brother wants to be in the band.

00:06:42.178 --> 00:06:45.000
You're right. Says Mick.
 
00:06:45.179 --> 00:06:48.340
Let's find someone new.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:53.171
Emma does not want to lose Al.

00:06:53.231 --> 00:06:57.292
She calls him on her mobile phone.

00:06:57.352 --> 00:06:59.846
Where are you?

00:06:59.906 --> 00:07:02.412
We're waiting for you.

00:07:02.472 --> 00:07:06.304
Get here fast and say sorry.

00:07:06.364 --> 00:07:10.978
Then perhaps we can forget these last weeks.

00:07:11.038 --> 00:07:14.131
But you must change Al.

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:17.293
You must give more time to the band.

00:07:20.095 --> 00:07:24.088
Al is in an internet cafe.

00:07:24.148 --> 00:07:27.974
He is trying to do his homework.

00:07:28.034 --> 00:07:33.129
Emma, things aren't easy for me these days.

00:07:33.189 --> 00:07:35.940
I can't work at home.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:39.262
Lisa's always crying.

00:07:39.321 --> 00:07:43.033
My parents are always with her.

00:07:43.093 --> 00:07:46.304
They tell me, do this.

00:07:46.364 --> 00:07:48.035
Do that.

00:07:48.095 --> 00:07:50.376
Now you're doing the same.

00:07:50.396 --> 00:07:53.800
Leave me alone.

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:59.940
And he stops the call and puts the phone down.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.612
Emma is very angry.

00:08:03.672 --> 00:08:10.684
I'm trying to help Al, but he's not interested, she thinks.

00:08:10.744 --> 00:08:15.006
She quickly sends him a phone message.

00:08:15.066 --> 00:08:20.374
Fast cars is looking for a new guitar player.

00:08:20.434 --> 00:08:23.061
Don't worry about us.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:26.391
We don't need you anymore, Al.

00:08:26.451 --> 00:08:27.482
Goodbye.

00:08:29.822 --> 00:08:34.123
Al tries to phone Emma, but she doesn't answer.

00:08:34.143 --> 00:08:37.384
How does he feel?

00:08:37.444 --> 00:08:39.095
Bad.

00:08:39.154 --> 00:08:43.126
He does not want to lose his friends.

00:08:43.185 --> 00:08:47.066
And he loves playing in the band.

00:08:47.126 --> 00:08:49.727
But what can he do now?

00:08:51.772 --> 00:08:55.753
Just then, his phone rings again.

00:08:55.813 --> 00:09:08.300
This time, it's his grandfather.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:26.900
Chapter Four. Something is wrong.

00:09:27.00 --> 00:09:29.400
Al does not answer his mobile, 

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:35.002
and his grandfather does not leave a message for him.

00:09:35.062 --> 00:09:38.893
I can phone him later. Al thinks.
 
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:45.658
When Al goes home, something is wrong.

00:09:45.718 --> 00:09:53.062
His mother's eyes are red, and his father's face is white.

00:09:53.122 --> 00:09:57.724
What's the matter? Al asks.
  
00:09:57.784 --> 00:10:01.695
It's your sister. Dad says.
 
00:10:01.755 --> 00:10:03.456
She's ill.

00:10:03.516 --> 00:10:05.116
Ill?

00:10:05.176 --> 00:10:08.478
Her heart isn't right, Al.

00:10:08.538 --> 00:10:12.370
She needs an operation and quickly.

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:13.800
Oh.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:15.720
There's more.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:18.472
It's a difficult operation.

00:10:18.532 --> 00:10:22.146
No hospital in England can do it.

00:10:22.206 --> 00:10:26.850
Lisa needs to go to the United States for it.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:28.722
I see.

00:10:28.782 --> 00:10:31.913
So, when are you going?

00:10:31.973 --> 00:10:34.124
We don't know.

00:10:34.184 --> 00:10:37.205
The operation's expensive.

00:10:37.265 --> 00:10:41.697
And there are the plane tickets and the hotel, too?

00:10:41.757 --> 00:10:44.878
Mr. Brown tries to smile.

00:10:44.938 --> 00:10:47.569
But we can find the money.

00:10:47.629 --> 00:10:50.036
Don't worry about it.

00:10:50.096 --> 00:10:54.966
Now Al is very sad and alone.

00:10:55.026 --> 00:10:59.100
Lisa is very ill, he knows.

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:02.882
Perhaps he can phone Emma.

00:11:02.942 --> 00:11:10.678
Then, on his mobile, he sees a message from his grandfather.

00:11:10.738 --> 00:11:13.970
Come and see me.

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:17.620
I know about Lisa.

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:21.590
Jack is waiting for Al.

00:11:21.650 --> 00:11:28.685
He is thinking about his sister, Alice, dead at 13.

00:11:28.745 --> 00:11:31.557
Suddenly, Al runs in.

00:11:33.819 --> 00:11:36.882
Granddad, what can we do?

00:11:36.942 --> 00:11:41.756
Where can we find the money for Lisa's operation?

00:11:41.816 --> 00:11:46.994
Take it easy, Al. Says Granddad. 
 
00:11:47.054 --> 00:11:50.019
I've got an idea.

00:11:50.079 --> 00:11:58.062
Tell your friends in the band, write a song for Lisa.

00:11:58.122 --> 00:12:00.774
A song for Lisa?

00:12:00.834 --> 00:12:03.094
How can that help?

00:12:03.154 --> 00:12:05.685
Trust me, Al.

00:12:05.746 --> 00:12:07.606
It can.

00:12:07.666 --> 00:12:11.908
Go home now and write your song.

00:12:24.528 --> 00:12:38.000
Chapter 5. Back to the Band.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:42.834
Back home, Al talks to his parents.

00:12:42.894 --> 00:12:46.556
I want to write a song for Lisa.

00:12:46.616 --> 00:12:49.880
I want to tell everyone about her.

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:53.339
Mr. and Mrs. Brown smile.

00:12:53.399 --> 00:12:56.176
What a nice idea.

00:12:56.236 --> 00:12:57.867
His mum says.

00:12:57.927 --> 00:12:59.227
Thanks, Al.

00:13:01.308 --> 00:13:03.698
Al phones his friends.

00:13:03.758 --> 00:13:07.479
He meets them at Ben's house.

00:13:07.539 --> 00:13:10.100
He says sorry.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:16.272
Then he tells them all about Lisa and the song.

00:13:16.332 --> 00:13:20.522
Emma looks at Mick and Ben.

00:13:20.582 --> 00:13:23.503
What do you think, boys?

00:13:23.563 --> 00:13:26.925
Can Al come back to the band now?

00:13:26.985 --> 00:13:28.776
She asks.

00:13:28.836 --> 00:13:32.259
Yes. Ben laughs.
 
00:13:32.319 --> 00:13:34.410
We need him.

00:13:34.470 --> 00:13:38.704
My brother can't play the guitar at all.

00:13:38.764 --> 00:13:41.696
And he can't write songs.

00:13:41.756 --> 00:13:43.606
Mick says.

00:13:43.666 --> 00:13:47.780
I've got an idea. Emma says.
 
00:13:47.839 --> 00:13:52.456
We can play Al's new song at our gig.

00:13:52.516 --> 00:13:55.719
What gig? Al asks.
 
00:13:55.779 --> 00:13:59.440
The gig for Lisa. Emma says.
 
00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:02.260
People can pay at the door.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:06.922
With their help, Lisa can have her operation.

00:14:06.982 --> 00:14:08.942
Good idea.

00:14:09.002 --> 00:14:11.623
Ben cries excitedly.

00:14:11.683 --> 00:14:16.746
Let's tell people about it on our website.

00:14:16.806 --> 00:14:25.172
So Mick puts the day and time of their next gig up on the band's website.

00:14:27.673 --> 00:14:34.736
Two weeks later, after lots of work, the band plays at Al's school.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:40.108
Al's family and friends are there.

00:14:40.168 --> 00:14:46.427
Late in the evening, Al sings Lisa's song.

00:14:46.487 --> 00:14:50.785
Some people from the radio are there too.

00:14:50.845 --> 00:14:52.556
They record the song.

00:15:02.559 --> 00:15:04.930
Let's sing for Lisa and her life.

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:07.451
The future's in her eyes are blue.

00:15:07.511 --> 00:15:09.742
A bright tomorrow's endless smile.

00:15:09.862 --> 00:15:23.523
So let's all help those times come true.

00:15:24.054 --> 00:15:31.050
Next day, Al and his friends look at the money from the gig.

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:33.812
How much is there?

00:15:33.872 --> 00:15:37.796
Can Lisa have her operation now?

00:15:37.856 --> 00:15:55.142
Chapter 6. Past concerts, future gigs.

00:16:05.908 --> 00:16:09.520
We need more money, Al says.

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:14.854
Then let's put Lisa's song on our website.

00:16:14.914 --> 00:16:16.344
Ben cries.

00:16:16.404 --> 00:16:20.702
People can pay for it and download it.

00:16:20.762 --> 00:16:25.808
People hear about Lisa's song on the radio.

00:16:25.868 --> 00:16:30.200
They pay and download it from the website.

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:35.312
Soon, Al's family have the money for America.

00:16:38.113 --> 00:16:42.934
At the airport, Al and his grandfather say goodbye.

00:16:45.575 --> 00:16:46.936
Good luck!

00:16:46.996 --> 00:16:50.177
Al calls to his parents and Lisa.

00:16:52.643 --> 00:16:58.948
Suddenly, Jack remembers a knight in 1941.

00:16:59.008 --> 00:17:01.772
His mother is dead.

00:17:01.832 --> 00:17:05.904
His father is away at the war.

00:17:05.964 --> 00:17:10.039
He is the man of the house now.

00:17:10.098 --> 00:17:17.205
Night after night, planes drop their bombs on their town.

00:17:17.265 --> 00:17:20.192
People are afraid.

00:17:20.252 --> 00:17:27.769
His sister, Alice, wants to sing and dance and forget the war.

00:17:27.829 --> 00:17:32.840
He hears her words that night and his answer.

00:17:32.901 --> 00:17:35.891
Please, can I go out, Jack?

00:17:35.951 --> 00:17:38.982
I want to sing at the concert.

00:17:39.042 --> 00:17:41.643
My friends are waiting.

00:17:41.703 --> 00:17:44.294
No, Alice.

00:17:44.354 --> 00:17:46.614
You're 13.

00:17:46.674 --> 00:17:49.332
You must stay at home.

00:17:49.392 --> 00:17:54.382
Later, he is working at the hospital.

00:17:54.442 --> 00:17:56.974
Bombs are dropping.

00:17:57.034 --> 00:17:59.774
The sky is red.

00:17:59.834 --> 00:18:06.898
Then someone says, Jack, there's a bomb in your street.

00:18:06.958 --> 00:18:09.169
Your house is on fire.

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:14.072
Alice, he cries.

00:18:14.132 --> 00:18:19.622
He runs home, but he can do nothing.

00:18:19.682 --> 00:18:22.790
He never sees Alice again.

00:18:25.691 --> 00:18:29.072
What's the matter, Grandad? Al asks.
 
00:18:30.152 --> 00:18:34.073
Jack smiles at his grandson.

00:18:34.133 --> 00:18:38.304
He sees a lot of Alice in the boy.

00:18:38.364 --> 00:18:44.125
Sometimes past experience teaches you things.

00:18:44.185 --> 00:18:49.484
Oh, it's not important now.

00:18:49.544 --> 00:18:54.606
But you must write some more songs.

00:18:54.666 --> 00:19:00.540
When's the band's next concert? Er, gig.
 
00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:02.874
Soon, Grandad.

00:19:02.934 --> 00:19:24.000
With that, Grandfather and grandson leave the airport and go home.
